---
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Container from '../Container.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../SectionHeader.astro';

/*
  Pitch page section 4 — what Gaia can't copy (docs/pitch-demo-sitemap.md §4.4).

  The shortest section on the page, and it stays that way: the rule once, its
  consequence once, no CTA. Its power is that it asks for nothing.

  The rule itself is not placeholder text — it is the project's binding rule as
  recorded in AGENTS.md and .claude/agents/README.md, quoted rather than
  re-invented here. The consequence paragraph is lorem ipsum pending
  `copywriter`.

  Gaia is described only as what it verifiably is — a subscription library of
  consciousness media. No claims about its numbers, its plans, or its quality:
  the sitemap's integrity note for this section is that a pitch attacking the
  incumbent reads as insecure, while one naming a thing the incumbent's
  architecture forbids reads as inevitable.

  Note for whoever builds /demo/*: this section is only true because the binding
  rule is enforced in the schema. `src/content/signals/` is still unregistered in
  src/content.config.ts and has no room field — registering it with a REQUIRED
  reference to an event is what makes this claim structural instead of
  aspirational. Out of scope for this pass; named here so it is not lost.
*/
---

<Section>
  <Container>
    <SectionHeader kicker="The moat" heading="What Gaia can't copy" />

    <p class="rule">
      Every piece of content resolves to a room — a dated, located gathering. If a piece of
      content can't say what room it leads to, it doesn't ship.
    </p>

    <p class="consequence">
      Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor
      incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud
      exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat.
    </p>
  </Container>
</Section>

<style>
  .rule {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    /* The rule is the section, so it is set as display type and given the whole
       measure; the consequence below it is deliberately quieter. */
    max-width: 26ch;
  }

  .consequence {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
</style>
